.IX Title "Clownfish::String 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::String 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::String \- Immutable string holding Unicode characters.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $string = Clownfish::String\->new(\*(Aqabc\*(Aq);
\&    print $string\->to_perl, "\en";
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = Clownfish::String\->new($perl_string);
.Ve
.PP
Return a String containing the passed-in Perl string.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS cat
.IX Subsection "cat"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string\->cat($other);
.Ve
.PP
Return the concatenation of the String and \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS to_i64
.IX Subsection "to_i64"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->to_i64();
.Ve
.PP
Extract a 64\-bit integer from a decimal string.  See \fBbasex_to_i64()\fR
for details.
.SS basex_to_i64
.IX Subsection "basex_to_i64"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->basex_to_i64($base);
.Ve
.PP
Extract a 64\-bit integer from a variable-base stringified version.
Expects an optional minus sign followed by base-x digits, stopping at
any non-digit character.  Returns zero if no digits are found.  If the
value exceeds the range of an \f(CW\*(C`int64_t\*(C'\fR, the result is undefined.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBbase\fR \- A base between 2 and 36.
.SS to_f64
.IX Subsection "to_f64"
.Vb 1
\&    my $float = $string\->to_f64();
.Ve
.PP
Convert a string to a floating-point number using the C library
function \f(CW\*(C`strtod\*(C'\fR.
.SS starts_with
.IX Subsection "starts_with"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string\->starts_with($prefix);
.Ve
.PP
Test whether the String starts with \f(CW\*(C`prefix\*(C'\fR.
.SS ends_with
.IX Subsection "ends_with"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string\->ends_with($suffix);
.Ve
.PP
Test whether the String ends with \f(CW\*(C`suffix\*(C'\fR.
.SS contains
.IX Subsection "contains"
.Vb 1
\&    my $bool = $string\->contains($substring);
.Ve
.PP
Test whether the String contains \f(CW\*(C`substring\*(C'\fR.
.SS find
.IX Subsection "find"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string_iterator = $string\->find($substring);
.Ve
.PP
Return a StringIterator pointing to the first occurrence of
\&\f(CW\*(C`substring\*(C'\fR within the String, or undef if the substring does not
match.
.SS length
.IX Subsection "length"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->length();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of Unicode code points the String contains.
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of bytes occupied by the String’s internal content.
.SS to_bytebuf
.IX Subsection "to_bytebuf"
.Vb 1
\&    my $byte_buf = $string\->to_bytebuf();
.Ve
.PP
Return a ByteBuf which holds a copy of the String.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one String is less than, equal to, or greater than
another.  The Unicode code points of the Strings are compared
lexicographically.  Throws an exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is not a String.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the Strings are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is less
than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS trim
.IX Subsection "trim"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string\->trim();
.Ve
.PP
Return a copy of the String with Unicode whitespace characters
removed from both top and tail.  Whitespace is any character that has
the Unicode property \f(CW\*(C`White_Space\*(C'\fR.
.SS trim_top
.IX Subsection "trim_top"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string\->trim_top();
.Ve
.PP
Return a copy of the String with leading Unicode whitespace
removed. Whitespace is any character that has the Unicode property
\&\f(CW\*(C`White_Space\*(C'\fR.
.SS trim_tail
.IX Subsection "trim_tail"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $string\->trim_tail();
.Ve
.PP
Return a copy of the String with trailing Unicode whitespace
removed. Whitespace is any character that has the Unicode property
\&\f(CW\*(C`White_Space\*(C'\fR.
.SS code_point_at
.IX Subsection "code_point_at"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->code_point_at($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Return the Unicode code point located \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR code points in from the
top.  Return \f(CW\*(C`CFISH_STR_OOB\*(C'\fR if out of bounds.
.SS code_point_from
.IX Subsection "code_point_from"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $string\->code_point_from($tick);
.Ve
.PP
Return the Unicode code point located \f(CW\*(C`tick\*(C'\fR code points counting
backwards from the end.  Return \f(CW\*(C`CFISH_STR_OOB\*(C'\fR if out of bounds.
.SS substring
.IX Subsection "substring"
.Vb 4
\&    my $result = $string\->substring(
\&        offset => $offset,  # required
\&        length => $length,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a new substring containing a copy of the specified range.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBoffset\fR \- Offset from the top, in code points.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBlength\fR \- The desired length of the substring, in code points.
.SS top
.IX Subsection "top"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string_iterator = $string\->top();
.Ve
.PP
Return an iterator initialized to the start of the string.
.SS tail
.IX Subsection "tail"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string_iterator = $string\->tail();
.Ve
.PP
Return an iterator initialized to the end of the string.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::String isa Clownfish::Obj.
